## Session 22 summary

**Criteria scope corrected (key reframe):** "2 node dlm=tcp test 100% successful" = the **full `./run.sh 2 tcp` suite** (16 tests; best prior 13/16, variable). dir_reuse_coherency is a deterministic proxy for the gating bug.

**Root cause CONFIRMED (RULE-4, live detectors — not guessing):** the clean-slate shutdown is **cross-node stale in-core INODE / BMAP** (the 90-session cache_coherency family):
- `P81-DEXT … verdict=incore-extent-stale` (in-core BMAP stale; on-disk free-space tree correct)
- `P47-INACT incore_gen=N disk_di_gen=N+1 disk_di_mode=00 verdict=DISK-FREE=>B-stale`
A stale in-core extent map (one incarnation behind disk) aliases a reused daddr → dir ino 131 reads daddr 0x78 = `/dev/urandom` file data → EFSBADCRC. **Ruled out:** allocator/bnobt double-alloc (sess55 detectors 0×), AG data-block partitioning, dir-format bugs. Confirmed against sess111/sess55/handoff memories.

**Strongest fix hypothesis (recorded):** `mxfs_buf_has_uncheckpointed_mods` (the P91-RELOAD-PROTECT gate at xfs_mxfs_dlm.c:5878) returns true on *any attached BLI* — the sess120 case-A/B contradiction applied to the **inode cluster** buffer — so a reload of a stale-live dir with a lingering BLI is **kept stale**, and the stale bmap survives. Fix direction: an exact li_lsn-vs-payload_lsn / coherent-plain-bio discriminator (as sess120 did for AG-meta) so a drained-on-disk advanced incarnation is *adopted*, not kept — without regressing genuine same-EX-tenure un-destaged work.

